---
/**
 * A hand-drawn pencil underline in the primary colour, for a short phrase in a heading. Wrap the
 * phrase in `<span class="relative">` and place this first, before its text:
 * `<span class="relative"><PencilUnderline />should, too</span>.` Prettier puts these on
 * separate lines; Astro's HTML compression (on by default) drops those line breaks, so no space
 * widens the underline. Coming first matters: as a positioned element the SVG counts as a block,
 * and accessible-name algorithms put a space around blocks, which would land before the period.
 *
 * It sits just under the Latin descenders. Mukta's line box is deeper than those letters, so the
 * stroke is lifted 0.2em from the bottom of the line (`top: calc(100% - 0.28em)`). Give the heading
 * about 0.1em of bottom padding so the stroke stays clear of whatever follows. It draws once, left
 * to right, on load (`animate-pencil-draw` in
 * src/styles/global.css); without motion it is simply there. Decorative: hidden from assistive
 * technology.
 *
 * The stroke joins round, like its caps. The curve has no corner, so this paints exactly as the
 * default miter join does, but Firefox sizes a stroked path's box for the sharpest possible miter
 * (the miter limit, 4, times half the stroke), so with a miter join it reports the line about two
 * stroke widths longer at each end than it draws.
 */
---

<svg
  class="pointer-events-none absolute top-[calc(100%-0.28em)] left-[-0.05em] h-[0.3em] w-[calc(100%+0.1em)] overflow-visible"
  viewBox="0 0 300 12"
  preserveAspectRatio="none"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <path
    class="stroke-primary motion-safe:animate-pencil-draw"
    d="M3 8.2C45 6.4 97 5.5 151 5.8S251 6.9 297 4.6"
    fill="none"
    stroke-width="2.6"
    stroke-linecap="round"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
    pathLength="1"
    stroke-dasharray="1 1.1"
  ></path>
</svg>
